# Auto-commit and deploy

After **any** code changes in this project — not only when the user asks — finish by committing and pushing:

1. Stage all changes: `git add -A`
2. Commit with a short descriptive message (HEREDOC format)
3. Push to origin (post-commit hook pushes automatically; Vercel deploys on push)

**Default: always do this.** Do not leave work uncommitted at the end of a task.

**Skip only when the user explicitly says not to** (e.g. "don't commit", "hold off on deploy", "WIP only").

**Do not commit** files that likely contain secrets (`.env`, credentials).

If the commit fails due to a pre-commit hook, fix the issue and create a **new** commit (do not amend unless hook rules allow).

After push, briefly confirm the commit hash in your reply so the user knows deploy is in progress.
